      "timestamp_raw": "Sept 21, 2016 15:26:09 GMT -5",
      "body_html": "<br/>Overall, this plant is a typical looking leucophylla with an extensive set of red veins carefully woven throughout the top of the trap.  Compared to other non-alba leucophyllas, the white on this plant is relatively bright.  It also can get very, very tall!    Here are some photos, taken 9/21/16:<br/><img src=\"https://c4.staticflickr.com/9/8511/29757608691_0eaeac489b_c.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"/><br/><br/><br/><img src=\"https://c3.staticflickr.com/9/8278/29727221482_d9a8b1fb85_c.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"/><br/><br/><img src=\"https://c3.staticflickr.com/9/8523/29547515730_64520b9be4_c.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"/><br/><br/><img src=\"https://c7.staticflickr.com/9/8813/29804850086_33beaea45e_c.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"/><br/><br/><img src=\"https://c3.staticflickr.com/9/8068/29804847426_8098a609df_c.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"/>",
